h sides).\n\n3. **The real discontinuity is in *which group members* are active.** Cohort A (114, 140, 182, 293, 356, 654) carries ~91 events each in the first half and drops to ~0\u20134 (step_05, step_09). Cohort B (731, 959, 1107, 1260, 1268, 1311) is silent in the first half and carries ~90 events each after 60074 (step_06, step_10).\n\n4. **Both cohorts talk to the same partners.** 182's neighbours pre-switch vs 731's post-switch overlap at **Jaccard \u2248 0.85** (step_07, step_08, step_15); 1107 shows the same roster (step_13). The external partners themselves simply rotate which hub they attach to (step_14) \u2014 their turnover is ~0.93\u20131.0 throughout, i.e. uniformly high background churn with no change point.\n\n5. **Volume is not the explanation either** \u2014 total group activity is roughly flat (~95\u2013110/bin) apart from a dip around 57574\u201362573 (step_02), which is the handover gap, not a partner replacement.\n\nThe prescribed 5000-unit before/after comparison shows an **old set of contacts persisting**, not giving way to a new one.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8155967f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [114, 140, 182, 293, 356, 654, 731, 959, 1107, 1260, 1268, 1311],\n  \"window\": [45074, 75074],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"narrative\": \"No abrupt change of interaction partners. With a 5000-unit half-window, group neighbourhood turnover peaks at only 0.33 and declines smoothly to ~0.14-0.21, with no isolated spike; the candidate peak time is unstable (54689 vs 57000) across window framings, indicating background drift. Edge-level Jaccard of 0.0 across the ~60074 split is an artifact of a MEMBER handover: cohort (114,140,182,293,356,654) goes from ~91 events each to ~0-4, while (731,959,1107,1260,1268,1311) goes from silent to ~90 each. Both cohorts contact essentially the same external roster (182 pre vs 731 post: Jaccard 0.85; 1107 confirms), so the contact set persists rather than being replaced. Confounder controls: total volume is flat (~95-110/bin) apart from the handover dip, and the external partners' own turnover is uniformly 0.93-1.0 across the whole period, i.e. high background churn with no change point.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 85895, "total_output_tokens": 7372, "total_tokens": 93267, "total_latency_ms": 107297, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}